---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Create a Connect account"
  description="Create an mdbase Connect account with a verified email address, then sync your first collection with Cloud copy or Private."
  current="connect"
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Create a Connect account</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">
      A Connect account syncs and shares your collections. One synced
      collection is free.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button button--primary" href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/signup">Sign up</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/login">Sign in</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="sign-up">
    <h2 id="sign-up">Sign up</h2>
    <p>
      Enter your email address, and Connect sends a one-time verification
      link. The link expires after one hour. Connect then asks for your name, a
      password, and your agreement to the service terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then choose <a href="/connect/#sync-options">Cloud copy or Private</a>{" "}
      for your first collection and open it in any <a href="/apps/">app</a>.
      Apps receive no access until you choose a collection and approve the
      operations they ask for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="beta-status">
    <h2 id="beta-status">Beta</h2>
    <p>
      Connect is in beta and has no availability guarantee. Keep independent
      backups of important collections.
    </p>
    <p>
      Accounts created during the beta keep their beta allowance, now counted
      in synced collections. An open-beta account can sync up to three
      collections and store 1 GiB, and each collection can be Cloud copy or
      Private.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="more">
    <h2 id="more">More information</h2>
    <p>
      Read <a href="/connect/">how Connect works</a> and{" "}
      <a href="/security/">what mdbase can read</a> in each option. The{" "}
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/terms/">service terms</a>{" "}
      apply when you create an account.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/spec/">mdbase specification</a> and local tools are open
      source and need no account. You can also{" "}
      <a href="/downloads/">download the desktop app</a> or{" "}
      <a href="/sdk/quickstart/">try the SDK</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
